<Layout title="SHARP · Space Array" active="sharp.html">

<main>
  <section class="hero"><div class="kicker">Candidate mission concept</div><h1>SHARP</h1><p class="lead">SHARP (Space-based High-resolution Array for Radio astronomy and Physics) is a proposed space-interferometry mission concept focused on ultra-high-resolution imaging of black holes and other compact astrophysical targets.</p></section>


<section class="proposal-hero">
  <a href="images/ESA-proposal_.jpg" target="_blank">
    <img src="images/ESA-proposal_.jpg"
         alt="Cover page of the SHARP ESA proposal">
  </a>

  <p class="image-caption">
    Cover page of the SHARP ESA M-class mission proposal.
  </p>
</section>

  <section class="two-col section">
    <div>
      <h2>Role within the Space Array roadmap</h2>
      <p>SHARP can be presented as a focused, scientifically compelling step toward the broader Space Array vision. It helps define the requirements, technologies, calibration strategies, and operational concepts needed for a future distributed observatory.</p>
      <h3>Key themes</h3>
      <ul class="clean">
        <li>High-frequency space VLBI and black-hole imaging.</li>
        <li>Precision baseline knowledge and orbit reconstruction.</li>
        <li>Calibration using astronomical sources and supporting metrology.</li>
        <li>Data handling, correlation, imaging, and science exploitation.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <aside class="card"><h3>Following content will be added later</h3><p>Mission summary, orbit concept, observing bands, expected angular resolution, target list, consortium information, proposal status, and links to public papers or presentations.</p></aside>
  </section>
</main>

</Layout>
